  "question": {
    "text": "A hydraulic automobile lift is designed to lift vehicles of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. The area of cross section of the cylinder carrying load is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. The maximum pressure the smaller piston would have to bear is [Assume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
  },
